<title>CANADA: William trades heavily after Swedish deal.</title>
<headline>William trades heavily after Swedish deal.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>William Resources Inc was heavily traded on the Toronto Stock Exchange on Tuesday after the mining company completed its takeover of Sweden's Terra Mining AB late last week.</p>
<p>&quot;We cemented our deal in Sweden,&quot; company spokesman Reg Burden said in a phone interview. &quot;Everything has been done and now we're ready to go out in January and produce gold, gold, gold. People are paying attention.&quot;</p>
<p>William Resources was flat at C$1.29, with more than 344,000 shares changing hands by mid-morning in a sluggish market.</p>
<p>Late last week, William Resources said shareholders of Terra Mining had overwhelmingly accepted its takeover bid.</p>
<p>((Heather Scoffield, Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8104))</p>
